   "num": "06",
   "kind": "short",
   "intro": "<p>In a field of sugar cane, gross primary production (GPP) is 1.80 × 10⁵ kJ m⁻² year⁻¹ and the plants' respiratory loss (R) is 8.1 × 10⁴ kJ m⁻² year⁻¹. Caterpillars of a moth bore into the stems and eat some of the net primary production (NPP). Farmers can spray an insecticide or release a parasitoid wasp, which lays its eggs inside the caterpillars. (Hypothetical data.)</p><figure><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%\"><table class=\"tbl\"><caption>Table 5</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit;padding:.3rem .4rem\">Treatment</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit;padding:.3rem .4rem\">NPP eaten by caterpillars / %</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit;padding:.3rem .4rem\">Cost / US$ ha⁻¹ year⁻¹</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit;padding:.3rem .4rem\">Predatory insect species</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit;padding:.3rem .4rem\">No treatment</th><td style=\"padding:.3rem .4rem\">12</td><td style=\"padding:.3rem .4rem\">0</td><td style=\"padding:.3rem .4rem\">14</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit;padding:.3rem .4rem\">Insecticide sprayed four times a year</th><td style=\"padding:.3rem .4rem\">2</td><td style=\"padding:.3rem .4rem\">160</td><td style=\"padding:.3rem .4rem\">5</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit;padding:.3rem .4rem\">Parasitoid wasp released once a year</th><td style=\"padding:.3rem .4rem\">3</td><td style=\"padding:.3rem .4rem\">70</td><td style=\"padding:.3rem .4rem\">13</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figcaption class=\"small\">Hypothetical data.</figcaption></figure>",
