     "model": "There are fewer blue-grey birds than the Hardy-Weinberg principle predicts, 120 compared with 168, and more black and white birds (220 compared with 196, and 60 compared with 36). This suggests that one of the conditions of the principle is not met, for example mating may not be random if breeders choose which birds mate. The difference only suggests this; a statistical test would be needed to show that it is significant.",
     "commonErrors": "Saying the principle is wrong; saying the difference proves non-random mating; comparing allele frequencies instead of genotype numbers."
