     "model": "When the breed fell to about 30 birds, only the alleles carried by those birds, 60 copies of each autosomal gene, were left, so many alleles were lost in this genetic bottleneck. The survivors carried only a chance sample of the original gene pool, so alleles that were rare before 1970 are likely to have been lost. New alleles only appear by mutation, which is rare, so the diversity does not come back even though the number of birds has risen.",
